e","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T21:43:05-07:00","id":561554,"title":"","content":"Oh, Tension Pools, Breaking Points, Alternate Forms - I like this sheet a lot! Will be great for new <b>Werewolf</b> players. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> But there is place for <b>both</b> Totem and Familiar? Even werewolves do not get both on their sheet...<br /> <br /> And minor point to make, <b>Gone</b> - the same thing as with mine sheet for Fae-Touched was - Tells are major things for Wolf-Blooded. In longer games, character can get a ew of them. I think that you can easily just cut a two lines on Aspirations ( <b>very</b> rare are players tha makes more than 4 of them per PC ) and one from Conditions - then add those three lines to Tells.<br /> <br /> I can easily imagine powerfull Wolf-Blooded character with 5 Tells. I have a problem to envision character with 6 Aspirations. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T22:23:26-07:00","id":561591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/466287-when-2ed-errata-and-char-sheets?p=561554#post561554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, Tension Pools, Breaking Points, Alternate Forms - I like this sheet a lot! Will be great for new <b>Werewolf</b> players. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> But there is place for <b>both</b> Totem and Familiar? Even werewolves do not get both on their sheet...<br /> <br /> And minor point to make, <b>Gone</b> - the same thing as with mine sheet for Fae-Touched was - Tells are major things for Wolf-Blooded. In longer games, character can get a ew of them. I think that you can easily just cut a two lines on Aspirations ( <b>very</b> rare are players tha makes more than 4 of them per PC ) and one from Conditions - then add those three lines to Tells.<br /> <br /> I can easily imagine powerfull Wolf-Blooded character with 5 Tells. I have a problem to envision character with 6 Aspirations. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Glad to hear you liked how it turned out!<br /> <br /> Well, I originally had room for about 4 tells(and space in the expanded Tells section for 4), but it was thought for now to keep it to two.<br /> <br /> Maybe I'll make an alternate version at some point that has room for more... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As for Familiars, I heard there was a tell that might grant a Familiar, so I was asked to include it....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":24,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","user":"Mr Gone","date":". 06-20-2015, 01:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T22:55:42-07:00","id":561606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/466287-when-2ed-errata-and-char-sheets?p=561554#post561554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, Tension Pools, Breaking Points, Alternate Forms - I like this sheet a lot! Will be great for new <b>Werewolf</b> players. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> But there is place for <b>both</b> Totem and Familiar? Even werewolves do not get both on their sheet...</div> </div> </div> </div>The Totem section is for the Pack Totem, since Wolf-Blooded can be full pack members and buy the Totem Merit. The Familiar section is for the Familiar Tell. It's very easy for even a starting Wolf-Blooded to have both.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/466287-when-2ed-errata-and-char-sheets?p=561554#post561554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And minor point to make, <b>Gone</b> - the same thing as with mine sheet for Fae-Touched was - Tells are major things for Wolf-Blooded. In longer games, character can get a ew of them. I think that you can easily just cut a two lines on Aspirations ( <b>very</b> rare are players tha makes more than 4 of them per PC ) and one from Conditions - then add those three lines to Tells.<br /> <br /> I can easily imagine powerfull Wolf-Blooded character with 5 Tells. I have a problem to envision character with 6 Aspirations. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>As Mr. Gone said, there was an earlier version with space for four Tells, but I suggested he remove them because it's currently not possible to have more than two Tells by RAW. You get one free Tell for being Wolf-Blooded, and you can gain a second by taking the Tell Merit, but as written, the Merit can't be taken multiple times. So for now, two is the limit. That's also why I asked for space for two alternate forms, since that's the most you could theoretically have, by taking Anger Issues and Shape-Shifted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T00:05:26-07:00","id":561643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/466287-when-2ed-errata-and-char-sheets?p=561606#post561606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As Mr. Gone said, there was an earlier version with space for four Tells, but I suggested he remove them because it's currently not possible to have more than two Tells by RAW. You get one free Tell for being Wolf-Blooded, and you can gain a second by taking the Tell Merit, but as written, the Merit can't be taken multiple times. So for now, two is the limit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I get the reading as letting you get just NEXT Tells. I will dwell in to mine 2ED corebook...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>TELL (\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>Wolf-Blooded<br /> <b>Effect:</b> The character develops a second Tell, chosen from those available to Wolf-Blooded. While the player chooses the new Tell, the character has no choice in how Father Luna or Mother Wolf\u2019s touch develops.<br /> With Storyteller permission, a human character can buy this Merit with Experiences to represent a character who spontaneously becomes Wolf-Blooded. </div> </div> </div>Well, it mentions second Tell, but do not indicate you are limit to only one. And it say that this Merit can be baught for non-Tells humans, to start WB templeate. I would rather let players to make exprianced WB with 3 or more Tells.<br /> <br /> Also, did not <b>Acrozatarim</b> in his <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/378460-a-werewolf-chronicle-in-paris\">Paris chronicle</a> do not get WB PC that had more Tells?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/378460-a-werewolf-chronicle-in-paris?p=393030#post393030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">The Pack</span></b><br /> Written-in-Blood, Blood Talon Rahu, a wasted life remade in a moment of carnage.<br /> Bianca Louvier, Storm Lord Irraka, scion of a noted lineage who stalked the stalker 'neath the new moon.<br /> Howling Phantom, Bone Shadow Ithaeur, woken to deeper truths beneath the skin of Paris.<br /> Henri, Wolf-Blooded, a conspiracy's favoured weapon fled from its sheathe.<br /> <br /> 1 Wolf-Blooded pack member who is involved with Written-in-Blood, expert on cults who fell into the Changeling's web.<br /> 6 human pack members, lost sheep formerly of the Changeling's flock who are now all too aware of the darkness in the world.<br /> <br /> <i>Zabarsimuhthari </i>the Enduring Smith of Bronze, spirit of a crumbling foundry whose doors have long since shut.</div> </div> </div> </div>From <a href=\"http://wiki.rpg.net/index.php/Werewolf_Paris/Henri\" target=\"_blank\">Henri's official sheet on games wiki</a>:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><b>Tells</b>:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><i>A Wolf's Meat</i> - Regenerates as a Primal Urge 1 Uratha, can spend Willpower to heal Lethal damage. Vulnerable to silver which stops healing; contact causes a rash and wounds are Aggravated.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><i>Familiar</i> - Empty Dust, a Hirsih contracted to his bloodline as guardian spirit.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><i>Piercing Eyes</i> - Can see Twilight creatures. Has striking, amber-coloured eyes which are hard to conceal.</span></span> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-20-2015, 03:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T02:47:26-07:00","id":561737,"title":"","content":"You, uh, you might want to not cut down below 5 Aspirations on the char sheet. No reason. Just sayin'.<br /> <br /> And yes, Henri in my Paris game has three tells and a pile of Experiences in order to bring him more in line with the Uratha characters. Normally a Wolf-Blooded can only have two Tells max but the world won't end if you go over that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T03:21:03-07:00","id":561750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/466287-when-2ed-errata-and-char-sheets?p=561737#post561737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You, uh, you might want to not cut down below 5 Aspirations on the char sheet. No reason. Just sayin'.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not remember when my players in three games based on GMC rules would have more than 4 Aspirations on the same time. Conditions also. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> There is just a limit on what people can track in the same time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/466287-when-2ed-errata-and-char-sheets?p=561737#post561737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yes, Henri in my Paris game has three tells and a pile of Experiences in order to bring him more in line with the Uratha characters. Normally a Wolf-Blooded can only have two Tells max but the world won't end if you go over that.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's why I advised more Tells - this WB sheet is for running WB in longer play. PC can take a Tell or three before his Tension ends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T07:15:54-07:00","id":561880,"title":"","content":"Normally Merits specify if they can be taken multiple times, and Tell does not. If you want to allow more than two Tells in your game that's fine, but by RAW it's not normally possible. That's why I requested the sheet the way I did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T09:41:43-07:00","id":562012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/466287-when-2ed-errata-and-char-sheets?p=561606#post561606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Totem section is for the Pack Totem, since Wolf-Blooded can be full pack members and buy the Totem Merit. The Familiar section is for the Familiar Tell. It's very easy for even a starting Wolf-Blooded to have both.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/466287-when-2ed-errata-and-char-sheets?p=561606#post561606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As Mr. Gone said, there was an earlier version with space for four Tells, but I suggested he remove them because it's currently not possible to have more than two Tells by RAW. You get one free Tell for being Wolf-Blooded, and you can gain a second by taking the Tell Merit, but as written, the Merit can't be taken multiple times. So for now, two is the limit. That's also why I asked for space for two alternate forms, since that's the most you could theoretically have, by taking Anger Issues and Shape-Shifted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the background on why we added Familiars and only two tells. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'm liking the debate though. For now I'll leave it at two, but I might see about maybe doing another version that has more at some point. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T05:22:09-07:00","id":562873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/466287-when-2ed-errata-and-char-sheets?p=562012#post562012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm liking the debate though. For now I'll leave it at two, but I might see about maybe doing another version that has more at some point. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Just before mine &quot;end of 2015/early 2016&quot; <b>Werewolf</b> game, when surely I will have at least one Wolf-Blooded PC. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And to be frank - it's rather small change ( I suspect, <b>Gone</b> ) so maybe let's look if sheet needs other tweaks, and when it will be finalized, just made two version of it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also - WB use Integrity in place of Harmony, even with Tension Pools option?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-21-2015, 10:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T06:33:42-07:00","id":562943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/466287-when-2ed-errata-and-char-sheets?p=561750#post561750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I do not remember when my players in three games based on GMC rules would have more than 4 Aspirations on the same time. Conditions also. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> There is just a limit on what people can track in the same time.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Juuuust trust me on this one. The character sheet is gonna need slots for 5 Aspirations. That's all I can say for now <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T08:06:58-07:00","id":563027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/466287-when-2ed-errata-and-char-sheets?p=562873#post562873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also - WB use Integrity in place of Harmony, even with Tension Pools option?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Why wouldn't they?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T17:01:48-07:00","id":563533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/466287-when-2ed-errata-and-char-sheets?p=562873#post562873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just before mine &quot;end of 2015/early 2016&quot; <b>Werewolf</b> game, when surely I will have at least one Wolf-Blooded PC. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'll see what I can do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/466287-when-2ed-errata-and-char-sheets?p=562873#post562873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And to be frank - it's rather small change ( I suspect, <b>Gone</b> ) so maybe let's look if sheet needs other tweaks, and when it will be finalized, just made two version of it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Not as small as you think, as I essentially have to remake that whole section. Acrobat isn't like Word sadly, so it takes a bit of work to rework a section like that.<br /> <br /> Not super hard mind you, but not as easy as you'd think...<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T21:01:01-07:00","id":563700,"title":"","content":"I thought that WB would have more akin to Harmony stat, as they could be <b>victims of botched Integrity roll in theirt place</b>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T21:28:32-07:00","id":563725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/466287-when-2ed-errata-and-char-sheets?p=563700#post563700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought that WB would have more akin to Harmony stat, as they could be <b>victims of botched Integrity roll in theirt place</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't understand what you mean. Could you please clarify?<br /> <br /> From the Wolf-Blooded section in Second Edition:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Character creation for Wolf-Blooded follows the rules in Making Monsters section of this book (p. 81) except where noted. Virtue and Vice : Wolf-Blooded characters, being mostly human, must select a Virtue and a Vice as per the character creation rules in The World of Darkness Rulebook or The God-Machine Chronicle .<br /> <b>Integrity : Wolf-Blooded characters do not have Harmony. Instead, they use the Integrity trait detailed in The World of Darkness Rulebook or The God-Machine Chronicle.</b><br /> Tells : Each Wolf-Blooded may select one Tell to start. Characters may purchase the Tell Merit to start with additional Tells. Having a Tell is what, essentially, makes a Wolf-Blooded a Wolf-Blooded.<br /> Wolf-Blooded Merits : Wolf-Blooded can select any Merits they have the prerequisites for, including the new Merits presented here. </div> </div> </div>Emphasis mine.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T23:14:47-07:00","id":563756,"title":"","content":"I was thinking here that Mortal character can become Wolf-Blooded with Dramatic Failure made on Lunacy roll. So they would have one Integrity point lower.","signature":"","edited":{"userid"